'''Tamodia''' is a sovereign state in [[Northern Meran]]. It borders [[Thyon]] to the south, [[Qym]] to the east, [[Nykal]] to the north, and [[Holaria]] to the west. 

==History==
*Populated by various tribes until the Iron Age.
*Conquered by the [[Cunerian Empire]] in {{abbr|350 BCE|290.75 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}}.
*The [[Sukats]] invade from the West in {{abbr|990 CE|822.42 CE (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. Becomes part of the [[Sukats Kingdom]], which wages wars against the [[Cunerian Empire]], notably incorporating the [[Duchy of Merin]] in {{abbr|1011 CE|839.86 CE (Earth Year Equivalent)}}.
*The [[Sukats Kingdom]] collapses in {{abbr|1100 CE|914 (Earth Year Equivalent)}} and the [[Western Sukatian Empire]] forms around Tamodia, with its capital in [[Mülahas]]. 
*The [[Western Sukatian Empire]] is progressively expelled from [[Thyon]] during the [[Thyo-Merinese Rejuvenation]]. 
*The [[Western Sukatian Empire]] formally collapses in {{abbr|1453 CE|1207 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, and is divided into various realms. The [[Principality of Tamodia]] is established. 
*The current Kingdom of Tamodia is established in {{abbr|1918 CE|1593 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, following [[SOME CONTINENTAL WAR]]. The Kingdom eventually becomes ruled by a cadet branch of the Qymish [[House of Zhifol]], after a series of succession rivalry with the Thyonese [[House of Ga]]. 
*Following the [[Prugundian Revolution]] and the subsequent [[Prugundian Civil War]], Tamodia becomes a constitutional monarchy in {{abbr|2197 CE|1825 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, ending [[wikipedia:absolutism|absolutism]]. 
*In {{abbr|2329|1935 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, Tamodia is invaded by [[Holaria]] which marks the beginning of the [[Boreal War]]. The country is decimated by the war, occupied for several years, and loses 28.6% of its pre-war population. 

